---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../../components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { COMPANY } from "../../../data/company";
---

<Layout
  title="DSCR Loans Explained: A Guide for Real Estate Investors | Cliffco Mortgage Bankers"
  description="How DSCR loans work, who qualifies, and why real estate investors use them to grow portfolios without relying on personal income documents."
  type="article"
>
  <Breadcrumbs trail={[
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "Learn", href: "/learn/" },
    { name: "DSCR Loans Guide", href: "/learn/dscr-loans-real-estate-investors-guide/" },
  ]} />

  <section class="container-wide pt-12 pb-12">
    <p class="eyebrow">DSCR</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3" style="font-size: var(--text-display-lg);">DSCR Loans Explained: A Guide for Real Estate Investors</h1>
    <p class="lead mt-6">
      DSCR loans qualify based on what the property earns, not what you earn. For investors who own
      multiple properties or have complex income, that distinction changes everything.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white pb-12">
    <div class="container-prose">

      <h2>What Is a DSCR Loan?</h2>
      <p>
        DSCR stands for Debt Service Coverage Ratio. It's a type of non-QM mortgage designed specifically
        for real estate investors. The defining feature is how it qualifies you: instead of looking at
        your W-2, tax returns, or personal income, the lender looks at the rental income of the property
        you're buying or refinancing. If the property generates enough cash flow to cover the debt
        payment, you qualify.
      </p>
      <p>
        This makes DSCR loans a natural fit for self-employed investors, business owners, and anyone
        growing a rental portfolio who doesn't want every new acquisition tied to personal income
        documentation.
      </p>

      <h2>How DSCR Is Calculated</h2>
      <p>The formula is straightforward:</p>
      <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-family: monospace; background: var(--color-mist-gray); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 6px;">
        <strong>DSCR</strong> = Gross Monthly Rent &divide; Monthly PITIA
      </p>
      <p>
        PITIA means Principal, Interest, Property Taxes, Insurance, and any HOA dues. A property
        renting for $2,500 per month with a total monthly payment of $2,000 has a DSCR of 1.25. Most
        programs want to see a DSCR of at least 1.0 to 1.25. Cliffco offers programs that go as low
        as 0.75 with compensating factors like a larger down payment or strong cash reserves.
      </p>

      <h2>What Are the Requirements?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>DSCR:</strong> 1.0 to 1.25 minimum for most programs; 0.75 with compensating factors</li>
        <li><strong>Credit score:</strong> 620 or above, with better pricing at higher scores</li>
        <li><strong>Down payment:</strong> 20% to 25%</li>
        <li><strong>Property type:</strong> Investment properties only. 1-to-4 unit residential, condos, and short-term rentals (Airbnb, VRBO) in eligible markets</li>
        <li><strong>Reserves:</strong> 3 to 6 months of payments in liquid accounts after closing</li>
        <li><strong>Entity vesting:</strong> Loans can close in an individual name or an LLC</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Eligible Property Types</h2>
      <p>
        DSCR loans work for a range of property types that conventional lenders sometimes won't touch:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Single-family rentals</li>
        <li>Condominiums (including non-warrantable condos through certain programs)</li>
        <li>2-to-4 unit residential properties</li>
        <li>Short-term rentals in markets where STR is legally permitted</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Primary residences are not eligible. DSCR is an investment-only product.
      </p>

      <h2>DSCR vs. Conventional Investment Loans</h2>
      <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
        <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 0.5rem;">
          <thead>
            <tr style="background: var(--color-mist-gray);">
              <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">Factor</th>
              <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">DSCR Loan</th>
              <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">Conventional</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">Qualification basis</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">Property rental income</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">Borrower personal income</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="background: var(--color-mist-gray, #f5f5f5);">
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">Income documents</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">None required</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">W-2s and tax returns</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">Eligible use</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">Investment only</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">Primary, second home, investment</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="background: var(--color-mist-gray, #f5f5f5);">
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">Down payment</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">20% to 25%</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist-gray);">3% to 5% (primary); 15%+ (investment)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Rates</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Higher than conventional</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Lower baseline rates</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Who Should Use a DSCR Loan?</h2>
      <p>DSCR loans tend to be the right fit for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Investors growing a portfolio and don't want each deal to require personal income re-verification</li>
        <li>Self-employed borrowers with complex tax returns that show low taxable income after deductions</li>
        <li>Business owners who keep personal and business finances separate and prefer not to expose personal financials for investment deals</li>
        <li>Short-term rental operators on Airbnb or VRBO who need a lender that understands STR income</li>
        <li>Out-of-state investors buying in markets like Orlando, Phoenix, or the Twin Cities</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Benefits</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No personal income documents required for qualification</li>
        <li>Can close in an LLC or personal name</li>
        <li>Covers long-term and short-term rentals</li>
        <li>Works for first-time investors and experienced portfolio builders</li>
        <li>Faster approval process than conventional investment loans in most cases</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Drawbacks to Understand</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Rates run higher than conventional investment loans</li>
        <li>Larger down payment required (20% to 25%)</li>
        <li>Fewer lenders offer DSCR than conventional products</li>
        <li>Not available for primary residences</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How the Process Works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Identify the property and get a sense of market rents (existing leases or a market rental analysis).</li>
        <li>Provide rental income documentation: signed leases, market rent analysis, or trailing 12-month operating statements for existing STRs.</li>
        <li>Submit credit authorization and down payment documentation.</li>
        <li>The lender calculates the DSCR and reviews the full file.</li>
        <li>Close. Most DSCR transactions close in 21 to 30 days.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Cliffco's DSCR program accepts short-term rental income for properties in eligible STR markets,
        including Disney-area Polk County in Florida, and can use market projection data for new STR
        purchases without an operating history.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="accent-gradient">
    <div class="container-wide py-16 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-white" style="font-size: var(--text-h2);">Ready to talk through your options?</h2>
      <p class="lead mt-4 text-white/85">A licensed Cliffco loan officer responds in one business day.</p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex justify-center gap-3 flex-wrap">
        <a href="/get-started/" class="btn btn-primary !bg-white !text-[var(--color-rich-black)]">Get a pre-qual</a>
        <a href={`tel:${COMPANY.hq.phoneE164}`} class="btn btn-secondary !border-white !text-white">{COMPANY.hq.phone}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
